## Router, less but right (open 2-5 files, never "read everything")

| Task | Read |
|---|---|
| Any session start | `MEMORY.md` (memory router), `HANDOFF.md` |
| Working a unit | `.claude/skills/{{FH_PROJECT}}/workflow.md` (canonical workflow) |
| Changing enforcement | `harness/adapter/adapter.yaml` (single source of truth) |

## Harness contract (enforced, not advisory)

- `make check` is the only definition of "done". `PROGRESS.yaml` items flip
  `passes: true` only on a green `make check` and must name their `evidence:`.
- The gate command is `.venv/bin/python harness/core/cli/gate.py`. Its verbs are
  `start`, `attempt <gate>`, `proceed`, `pending`, `status` and `verify`. Each refusal
  prints the command to run next.
- A gate passes only through its checks (`attempt`) or an answered approval (`proceed`).
  Nothing sets a gate by name.
- Evidence over opinion: no gate advances without the artifact its checks read.
- Do not edit files under `harness/core/`: they are template-owned (`gategraph update`
  syncs them). Project enforcement grows in `harness/adapter/` and `packs/`.
- Run `make venv` once before the first gate command (it builds `.venv` from the lock).

